WEBVTT

title
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.081
Entities: how entities work.

what-typed
00:00:03.281 --> 00:00:08.326
An entity is a typed record,
with the fields its type defines.

what-id
00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:15.222
It has an ID people can read,
ABY-000001, and it’s kept in a project.

examples-types
00:00:16.422 --> 00:00:21.467
Plugins define the types, each
with its own ID prefix and fields.

custom-plugin
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:28.452
A lab can add its own entity
types, in a plugin of its own.

custom-manifest
00:00:28.452 --> 00:00:33.867
The type lists its fields, what
makes two the same, and its rules.

identity-same
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:39.370
Two antibodies with the same
chains are the same antibody.

identity-found
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:45.156
Registering them again finds ABY-000001:
the project gets its own record.

history-revisions
00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:51.770
Every change makes a new revision:
who, when, how, and any reason given.

history-kept
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.333
Revisions can’t be changed
or removed, by anyone.

history-signed
00:00:55.333 --> 00:01:00.748
Releasing a lot takes QA’s signature:
a fresh sign-in, tied to that revision.

triggers-registered
00:01:01.948 --> 00:01:07.733
A trigger runs an action when an entity
changes, such as registering a protein.

triggers-consent
00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:12.778
Withdrawing a donor’s consent can
hold what was made from their samples.

triggers-admin
00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:18.933
Triggers are off until a project Admin
turns them on. Each run names its trigger.

lineage-links
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:26.289
An entity links to its lots, the runs
that used it, and what they made.

close
00:01:27.489 --> 00:01:31.422
Entities are the records
actions work on. Next: actions.
